# Force LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Why a catch-all: the compiler emits the artefacts (manifest.json, the
# two SBOMs, vex, provenance) with LF newlines on every OS, and a
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites any text file not pinned
# here to CRLF. Pinning every tracked file to eol=lf makes the working
# tree LF regardless of the contributor's autocrlf setting, so:
#   - main.capa hashes the same bytes the CI sees, and
#   - if you opt into committing an artefact snapshot (see .gitignore),
#     a regenerated file does not differ from it in line endings alone.
#
# Every tracked file in this repo is text (.capa, .json, .md, .toml,
# LICENSE); there are no binaries, so a blanket eol=lf is safe. If a
# binary asset is ever added, give it an explicit `*.ext binary` rule
# below to opt it out.
* text=auto eol=lf
